    "description": "Renewa acquires and manages land interests under utility-scale renewable-energy projects. Its customers are renewable developers, project owners, and infrastructure investors that need long-duration land control rather than conventional project-level equipment financing. The business is contract-based and infrastructure-linked because value depends on long-term ground leases and site-control arrangements under operating and planned clean-energy projects. CDPQ stated in 2025 that Renewa had attracted more than $750 million of funding commitments since its inception in 2022. Its principal operating footprint is in the United States. CDPQ announced a $200 million investment in July 2025 alongside QIC-backed ownership, and public materials reviewed do not disclose the current ownership percentages.",
